@page {
    meta: {
        title: "Write documentation components",
        description: "Author asides, steps, includes, and no-JS tabs in Rocdown without raw HTML.",
    },
}

# Write documentation components

Use `@docs` for bounded documentation components. The parser stores the kind
and body; Rocdown validates the content model; the theme paints the HTML. Fenced
code stays display-only.

@docs note {
    title: "Static pages"

    Rocdown accepts `@docs` next to Markdown and `@page`. `@render`, `@roc`, and
    other islands still require `rocci run`.
}

## Call out a risk

@docs caution {
    Do not paste raw HTML into Markdown. Use a component when the page needs
    structure beyond CommonMark.
}

## Walk through a procedure

@docs steps {
    @docs step {
        title: "Author the directive"

        Start a document-root line with `@docs`, then the kind, then a brace
        body. Nested `@docs` are allowed. Write `\@docs` for a literal example.
    }

    @docs step {
        title: "Include source from disk"
        verify: Bool.true

        Point `@docs include` at a file under the content root. Prefer a named
        region over line numbers.
    }
}

@docs include {
    path: "snippets/hello.rs"
    region: "hello"
    language: "rust"
}

## Show alternatives without JavaScript

Every tab panel is in the document. Print, forced-colors, and browsers with
scripts disabled show all panels. There is no `tablist` role until a hashed
script exists.

@docs tabs {
    group: "install"
    kind: "tool"

    @docs tab {
        id: "cli"
        label: "CLI"

        Check the catalog without compiling Roc:

        ```sh
        cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- check docs
        ```
    }

    @docs tab {
        id: "test"
        label: "Examples"

        Run declared example commands. This is not part of `rocdown build`.

        ```sh
        cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- test docs
        ```
    }
}

## Link related pages

@docs card-grid {
    @docs link-card {
        page: "reference/rocdown"
    }

    @docs link-card {
        page: "reference/rocdown-site"
    }
}

@docs example {
    id: "echo-hello"
    language: "sh"
    test: ["/bin/echo", "hello"]
    expect: "hello"

    ```sh
    echo hello
    ```
}

## Embed an interactive playground

Embed an in-browser WebAssembly compiler that allows readers to edit and inspect `.rocci` templates and `.rocdown` documents live:

````rocdown
@docs playground {
    id: "counter"
}
````

Rocdown site compilation automatically detects pages containing `@docs playground`, bundles self-hosted hashed assets (`playground-app.js`, `playground-worker.js`, `styles.css`, `compiler.wasm`), and generates page-scoped Content Security Policies (`script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'`). All other documentation pages remain script-free with strict `script-src 'none'`.

`api-operation` is reserved for generated API reference and is rejected until
that work ships.
